1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Heinrick Wassmuth was my husband, Don's, great grandfather.  Family lore ( I haven't check the truth) says that Heinrick's parents were not married.  One of his parents was Catholic and the other Lutheran!!  We hav
2 CONC e been told that his natural father's name was Risse, I'm not sure if that is true or not.  There was no way either parents would allow a marriage so when she found out she was pregnant she had Heinrick out of wedlock on 27 Nov 18
2 CONC 37 in Westphalen, Germany.  She later married Johanas Kulemeyer, but Heinrick did not like his step-father.  According to St. Anthony Church Centennial 1858 - 1958 from Effingham, Illinois.  Heinrick came to the United States in 1
2 CONC 856 from Westphalen, Germany.  I found him first in St. Clair County, Illinois where he married Mary FRANKE  9 Feb. 1863 in St. Liborius Catholic Church in ST. Libory, Illinois.  Heinrick and Mary had one child, Anna born 10 May 1
2 CONC 864 in Effingham, Illinois, she died 24 May 1864 in Effingham, Illinois.  Mary A. died 20 May 1864.  Heinrick married 2nd Mary Ann Hoffman, who had emigrated from Oldenburg, Germany in 1851.  They were married 16 Aug 1864 in Effin
2 CONC gham, Illinois.  Mary Ann Hoffman was born 14 Feb 1843 in Oldenburg, Germany.  They had 9 children.  Elizabeth born 19 Jan 1866 in Effingham, Illinois, Mary born 07 Dec 1867 in Effingham, Illinois, Catherine born 16 Aug 1870 in Ef
2 CONC fingham, Illinois, Dorothy born 15 Nov. 1872 in Effingham, Illinois, Henry H. born 02 Aug 1875 in Effingham, Illinois, Louise born 18 May 1877 in Effingham, Illinois, Clemens J. born 27 Sept 1880 in Effingham (Don's grandfather), 
2 CONC Anthony J. born 01 Mar 1884 in Effingham, Illinois and Mary Ann born 21 May 1889 in Effingham, Illinois.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the book I previously quoted, The Wassmuth family lived north of St. Anthony rectory, at the corner of Virginia and Third streets until 1878 when they moved to a farm three miles north of Effingham.  Later the family 
2 CONC moved to Idaho.   Henry Wassmuth worked on the present church from start to finish.  He erected the first cross on the tower.  With Anton Schleper he built the side altars and the pews.  This article says that there were 10 childr
2 CONC en.
2 CONT
2 CONT I wrote to the church in 2001 asking for information on the baptisms of the children, it listed the following children: Mary Ann born May 20, 1889 and baptized May 21, 1889, Marie Anna baptized January 19, 1866, Mary baptized Dece
2 CONC mber 8, 1867 and born December 7, 1867, Anna Mary Catherine baptized August 19, 1870 and born Aug. 16, 1870, Herman Henry baptized on Aug 2 and born Aug 2, 1875, Louise Anna baptized May 19, 1878 and born May 18, 1878, Clemens Jos
2 CONC eph born Sept 28, 1880 baptized Sept 29, 1880, and Anthony born Mar 1, 1884 and baptized Mar 7, 1884.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sally Wassmuth 7-26-2011
