1 NAME John Louis /Reinertson/
2 GIVN John Louis
2 _MARNM Reinertson
2 NICK John Lewis
2 NICK Louie
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 29 DEC 1889
2 ADDR
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 3 JAN 1976
2 ADDR
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Louis Reinertson, mayor of Kelley, Iowa.
2 CONT
2 CONT He went by "Louie" much of the time informally in the community, actual correct name from confirmation certificate was John Louis Reinertson, but in many minor social or casual newspaper references they listed him as Lewis or Loui
2 CONC s.
2 CONT
2 CONT He has many public notices in the newspapers, since for the little town of Kelley, Iowa he was the mayor and often the Justice of the Peace, an office which acted as a Judge for minor infractions such as traffic infractions and co
2 CONC uld legally perform marriages, etc. These were routinely reported in the local newspapers.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married  Mabel Heggem from Slater Iowa and briefly lived with the in-laws until the birth of Arlene Reinertson Harrison (later of Santa Cruz, California).
2 CONT
2 CONT Later he lived in Oskaloosa, working rail yard for Chicago Northwestern railroad for some years after he first married. Faye Reinertson Hanna of San Luis Obispo California was born then. He lived most of his life in Kelley Iowa, u
2 CONC ntil he became unable to live alone and went to live with his son in Ocheyedan Iowa for a couple years, then when he became very weak and needed constant care he was in a nursing home briefly in Milford Iowa and then in Lake Park 
2 CONC Iowa, both very near Ocheyedan.  He also spent a few months in Bethesda Nursing home in Story City, which explains most of the references to other dwellings.
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived and farmed in Lamberton Minnesota in the 1920's for approximately ten years. He then moved back to Kelley and lived there until he became too infirm in the mid 1970's.
2 CONT
2 CONT Information from grandson John Reinertson.
