1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/128134412/alvin-e-orsted
2 CONT
2 CONT Excerpted & edited obituary from Hansen Family Funeral Services (names of possibly living survivors redacted):
2 CONT
2 CONT "Alvin E. Orsted, 78, Green Bay lost a 32 year fight with non-Hodgkin's Lymphoma on Sunday, November 23, 2008 at home. Alvin was born to Gardner and Tracy (Schram) Orsted on December 25, 1929 at Bailey's Harbor, WI. On June 9, 195
2 CONC 1, Alvin married Dixie Ann Peil at St. Mary of the Lake Church in Bailey's Harbor. Upon discharge as a Korean War Veteran, he went to work at Hoberg's (Charmin/P&G) until retirement on disability due to Cancer in 1984. Al ushered 
2 CONC at St. Willebrord's for many years. He also served as a Sheriff's Deputy in the 1970's. Al Belonged to the Bellevue V.F.W. Post #9677.
2 CONT
2 CONT "... surviving are sisters, ... Elaine (Ed) Zahn ...; brothers: Dale, Orval ...; sister-in-law, Delores ...
2 CONT
2 CONT "Al was preceded in death by pre-born twin daughters and daughter Lisa B. Anderson; grandson, Jamie; pre-born grandson, Presley; brothers: John, Edward, twins Earl and Irvin [Ervin F. Orsted]; sister-in-law: Marie: in-laws: Art, F
2 CONC ay and Patrick Peil.
2 CONT
2 CONT "According to his wishes, Al's cremains will be inurned at a later date in the Bailey's Harbor Cemetery."
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT Cremated
