1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Funeral services for Thora Haaland, 77, Cooperstown, were held October 2 at Trinity Lutheran Church in Cooperstown. Interment was in the Ness Cemetery, rural Cooperstown. She died September 27, 1997, in the Griggs 
2 CONC County Hospital in Cooperstown.
2 CONT Thora Stangeland was born July 1, 1920, in Stavanger, Norway, the daughter of Tonnes and Inga (Fiestad) Stangeland.
2 CONT She married Knute Haaland December 30, 1942 in Norway. They came to North Dakota in 1947, residing in the Valley City area until 1958. They then moved to Litchville, where they farmed until 1969. They moved to Cooperstown, where T
2 CONC hora worked as a cook and waitress in the Moline Café and as a nurses aid in the Griggs County Hospital, retiring in 1988. Knute died September 27, 1989, and Thora continued to make her home in Cooperstown.
2 CONT She is survived by: one son, Irwin, of Cooperstown; two daughters, Judy (Dan) Paintner of Cooperstown, Karen Haaland of Fargo; 11 grandchildren; two great-grandchildren.
2 CONT She was preceded in death by here parents and three sons, Kaare, Alfred, Torleif (Ted); three brothers: Ole, Toralf; Ommund; four sisters; Anna, Margrethe, Kari and Ingrid.
2 CONT Published in the Griggs County Sentinel-Courier, Cooperstown, North Dakota, October 3, 1997.
2 CONT
